# §3. GP-AUD-017 ask 1 — the compensation polynomial, and a catch

## §3.1 The polynomial

Add the quartic \(Q_4=\frac{c_{40}}{24}x^4+\frac{c_{31}}6x^3y+\frac{c_{22}}4x^2y^2
+\frac{c_{13}}6xy^3+\frac{c_{04}}{24}y^4\) to the cubic model. On the axis:
\(Q_4(x,0)=\frac{c_{40}}{24}x^4\), \(\partial_xQ_4(x,0)=\frac{c_{40}}6x^3\),
\(\partial_yQ_4(x,0)=\frac{c_{31}}6x^3\). The six pin violations at
\((\pm r/2,0)\) are cancelled exactly by

\[
\boxed{\ \delta(x,y)=\frac{c_{40}\,r^4}{384}
\;-\;\frac{c_{40}\,r^2}{48}\,x^2
\;-\;\frac{c_{31}\,r^2}{24}\,xy\ }
\]

**Verification.** Values: \(Q_4(\pm r/2,0)=c_{40}r^4/384\);
\(\delta(\pm r/2,0)=\frac{c_{40}r^4}{384}-\frac{c_{40}r^2}{48}\frac{r^2}4
=-c_{40}r^4/384\) ✓. Gradients: \(\delta_x=-\frac{c_{40}r^2}{24}x\to\mp c_{40}r^3/48\)
against \(\pm c_{40}r^3/48\) ✓; \(\delta_y=-\frac{c_{31}r^2}{24}x\to\mp c_{31}r^3/48\)
against \(\pm c_{31}r^3/48\) ✓. Six conditions, six checks. \(c_{22},c_{13},c_{04}\)
never violate the pins (their axis restrictions vanish to the needed order) and need
no compensation. \(\delta\) is the unique compensation in
\(\mathrm{span}\{1,x^2,xy\}\) — the canonical minimal-degree gauge; other gauges
exist and differ only by re-parametrizing the sampled jets.

**Scaling order — the structural payoff.** \(Q_4(rX,rY)=r^4\tilde Q_4\) and
\(\delta(rX,rY)=r^4\tilde\delta\), so the full model is
\(f=b+r^3[\tilde P+r(\tilde Q_4+\tilde\delta)]\): **quartics enter the scaled
dynamics as an O(r) perturbation of the r-free cubic flow.** Away from the
degenerate layer the classification is structurally stable, so the complements
inherit only \((1+O(r))\) modifications — the \(r\) and \(r^3\) laws survive.
What this sketch does *not* cover is the failure layer itself, where the transverse
eigenvalue degenerates and structural stability fails; there an O(r) perturbation
can shift the constant but a *power* change would require it to scale anomalously
on that layer, which it does not. This is the same boundary-layer uniformity gap as
the manuscript's §11, relocated — labeled a sketch, not a theorem.

**Frozen thresholds for the Q4-on run.** I co-sign GP-AUD-017's tripwire: a weighted
complement above ~10⁻⁴ at r=0.025 is a qualitatively new mechanism and my sketch is
wrong. Additionally: if the sketch holds, the Q4-on weighted value at r=0.025 should
sit within an \(O(r)\)-sized band — tens of percent, not orders of magnitude — of
the cubic 1.186×10⁻⁸. Between those markers (say 10⁻⁷–10⁻⁵): inconclusive, report
without fitting.

## §3.2 The catch — the quartic jets must be sampled conditionally

**Sampling \((c_{40},\ldots,c_{04})\) from the stationary law would mis-specify the
experiment at O(1), not O(r).** The registry-#5 battery gives, for the normalized BF
covariance \(K=e^{-|u|^2/2}\) (single point, \(\mathrm{Cov}(\partial^\alpha f,
\partial^\beta f)=(-1)^{|\beta|}\partial^{\alpha+\beta}K(0)\), entries
\((-1)^{m+n}(2m-1)!!(2n-1)!!\)):

\[
\mathrm{Var}(c_{40})=\mathrm{Var}(c_{04})=105,\quad
\mathrm{Var}(c_{31})=\mathrm{Var}(c_{13})=15,\quad
\mathrm{Var}(c_{22})=9,
\]
\[
\mathrm{Cov}(c_{40},c_{22})=15,\quad \mathrm{Cov}(c_{40},c_{04})=9,\quad
\mathrm{Cov}(c_{40},f)=3,\quad \mathrm{Cov}(c_{40},f_{xx})=-15 .
\]

That last pair is the problem: the quartic jets are even-order and correlate with
the *pinned* even jets. Conditioning on \(f=b\) alone already gives
\(E[c_{40}\mid f=b]=3b=3.6\) — against a conditional σ of ~10, a real shift, and
\(c_{22},c_{04}\) shift likewise. The odd-order cubic jets \((a,w,z)\) stay
uncorrelated with the quartics at a point (odd total order), so *their* sampling is
unaffected. By x-parity within the pin set, \(E[c_{31}\mid\text{pins}]=
E[c_{13}\mid\text{pins}]=0\) — the two coefficients that enter \(\delta\)'s odd part
are mean-zero, but their variances still contract.

**Recipe:** build the 11-dimensional stationary covariance of
\((\text{six coalesced pin jets};\,c_{40},c_{31},c_{22},c_{13},c_{04})\) from the
double-factorial table, Schur-complement onto the quartic block given the pin
values \((b,-\kappa/6,0,0,0,0)\), and sample the five quartics from that conditional
Gaussian. Mechanical but fiddly. **Offer: I will grind the full 11-dim Schur
complement into explicit conditional means and a 5×5 covariance next round if GP
wants it pre-checked before implementation** — this is exactly the closed-form lane
I keep advertising.

